#: src/whatis.php:34 src/whatis.php:38 src/MultiFlexi/Ui/MainMenu.php:55
msgid "What is MultiFlexi?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce que MultiFlexi ?"

#: src/whatis.php:40
msgid ""
"MultiFlexi is an open-source task scheduling and automation platform for "
"business system integrations. It lets organizations run applications — "
"importers, exporters, reports, health checks — on a schedule across multiple "
"companies, with isolated credentials and full execution history."
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:46
msgid "MultiFlexi dashboard"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:51
msgid ""
"Think of it as cron on steroids for business automation: instead of managing "
"scattered shell scripts and cron entries, you register applications once, "
"assign them to companies with the right credentials, and let MultiFlexi "
"handle scheduling, execution, output capture, and monitoring."
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:56
msgid "Who is it for?"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:60
msgid "Accounting Firms"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:60
msgid ""
"Automating daily tasks for dozens of clients — bank imports, invoice "
"generation, report exports — each running with that client's own credentials."
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:61
msgid "Managed Service Providers"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:61
msgid ""
"Running system health checks, backup verifications, and compliance reports "
"across customer environments on schedule."
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:62
msgid "Internal IT Teams"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:62
msgid ""
"Synchronizing data between systems, dispatching notifications, and "
"maintaining databases without hand-written automation glue."
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:77
msgid "Key Concepts"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:79
msgid "MultiFlexi is built around five core entities that work together:"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:85
msgid "MultiFlexi entity relationships"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:91
msgid "Company"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:91
msgid ""
"A tenant or organization you automate tasks for. Each company has its own "
"set of credentials and job history, ensuring full data isolation."
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:92
msgid ""
"A tool that MultiFlexi can execute — a CLI binary, a PHP script, a Docker "
"image. Applications are registered once and can be assigned to any company."
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:93
msgid "Credential"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:93
msgid ""
"Securely stored authentication data (API keys, database passwords, SMTP "
"accounts). Credentials are scoped to a company and encrypted at rest with "
"AES-256."
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:94
msgid "RunTemplate"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:94
msgid ""
"The link between an application and a company: \"run this app for this "
"company on this schedule with these credentials.\""
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:95
msgid "Job"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:95
msgid ""
"A single execution of a RunTemplate. MultiFlexi records the start time, exit "
"code, stdout, stderr, and any output files as searchable artifacts."
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:114
msgid "How It Works"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:117
msgid ""
"Register an application — import its JSON definition or create it in the web "
"UI."
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:118
msgid ""
"Add a company — create a tenant representing the organization whose tasks "
"you're automating."
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:119
msgid ""
"Assign credentials — store the company's API keys, database passwords, or "
"SMTP accounts. MultiFlexi encrypts them and injects them as environment "
"variables at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:120
msgid ""
"Create a RunTemplate — pick the application, the company, the schedule, and "
"the credentials."
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:121
msgid ""
"Jobs run automatically — the scheduler daemon creates job records when the "
"schedule is due, and the executor daemon launches the application and "
"captures all output."
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:133
msgid "Execution Environments"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:135
msgid "MultiFlexi can launch applications in several ways:"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:141
msgid "Native"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:141
msgid "run the command directly on the server"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:142
msgid "Docker"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:142
msgid "run inside a Docker container with the application's OCI image"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:143
msgid "Podman"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:143
msgid "rootless container execution"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:144
msgid "Kubernetes"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:144
msgid "launch as a K8s pod"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:145
msgid "Azure Container Instances"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:145
msgid "run in the cloud"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:158
msgid ""
"The executor is pluggable: each RunTemplate can use a different execution "
"backend depending on the application's requirements."
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:163
msgid "Multiple Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:165
msgid ""
"You interact with MultiFlexi through whichever interface fits your workflow:"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:170
msgid "Web UI"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:170
msgid ""
"Bootstrap 5 dashboard with real-time metrics, company/application/credential "
"management, job history, and live output streaming via WebSocket."
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:171
msgid "CLI"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:171
msgid ""
"Full-featured command-line tool for scripting, CI/CD pipelines, and headless "
"administration."
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:172
msgid "TUI"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:172
msgid ""
"Interactive terminal interface built with Bubbletea (Go) for keyboard-driven "
"management."
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:173
msgid "REST API"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:173
msgid ""
"JSON/XML/YAML endpoints with HTTP Basic and token authentication for "
"programmatic integration."
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:174
msgid "MCP Server"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:174
msgid "Model Context Protocol server for AI agent integration."
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:191
msgid "Monitoring and Observability"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:195
msgid ""
"Zabbix integration with Low-Level Discovery — auto-discovers companies and "
"applications, monitors job success rates and execution times"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:196
msgid "OpenTelemetry support for distributed tracing"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:197
msgid "Structured logging to syslog, database, and custom targets"
msgstr ""

#: src/whatis.php:198
msgid ""
"Universal artifact preservation — every job's stdout, stderr, and output "
"files are stored and searchable"
msgstr ""

